                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of south central New Mexico, including Sacramento\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Saturday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Several rounds of thunderstorms are expected to move through the\nSacramento Mountains between this evening and late Saturday\nnight. Widespread rainfall amounts of 1\" are likely with\nlocalized areas receiving 2-3\" resulting in flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
