                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 23 at 5:44PM MDT until October 24 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible although the risk will decrease into the evening as\nstronger showers and thunderstorms diminish.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may exacerbate flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Waves of showers and isolated embedded thunderstorms will\ncontinue into the evening.  Although rainfall will be more\nlimited in coverage, localized amounts of up to 0.5 inches could\ncause additional minor rises in the smaller creeks and\ntributaries.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley with\nthe greatest risk across Conejos County.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible new\nFlood Warnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be\nprepared to take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
